jsx - javascript xml
jsx rules
it must have one parent
className
camelCase
tag must be closed
{} can be written
terinary operator
<></> 
style={{ backgroundColor: 'skyblue', padding: '10px' }}
component must have a capital letter at starting


component
it renders the part of UI that can be reusable
class components - life cycle methods
functional componets - Hooks


cards

props
props is a immutable objects
it is used to pass the data from parent to child

destructuring
it is a process of extracting values
from object and array and assiging it 
to varaiables

let obj={
   name:'john',
   city:'vizag'

}
let {name,city}=obj
console.log(city)


in react 
webpage will not rerender when the variable changes
it will only rerender whenever the state changes

state
it is also like a variable which stores the dynamic data related to the component

Hooks - built in functions
1) useState
it is used to manage the state values

syntax
import {useState} from 'react';

let [state,setState]=useState(intitialvalue)

state- it is state variable name
setState- it is used to update the state value
useState- hook 
initialvalue - "" or [] or {} or data

let [val,setVal]=useState('hello')

setVal('hi')
setVal('hello world')

{val}


form handling in react
1) uncontrooled form handling - useRef
2) controlled form handling -it is controlled by react using e.target.value



useEffect
it is used to manage the side effects such as api calling,localstorage and timers
1) useEffect with no dependency - it will run whenever the state changes
2) useEffect with [] dependency array- it will run only one time
3) useEffect with dependency value - it will run one time  and rerun when the dependency changes

import {useEffect} from 'react';

useEffect(()=>{
   console.log('api logic')
})

useEffect(()=>{
   console.log('api logic')
},[])


useEffect(()=>{
   console.log('api logi')
},[val])


how to render a list 
using map we can reder list

key
key is used to identify the item unique for updation and deletion



routing 
react router dom
it is library that is used to integrate routing 


static routing
1) npm install react-router-dom

2) integrate in main.jsx

import {BrowserRouter} from 'react-router-dom'

<BrowserRouter>
<App/>
</BrowserRouter>


3) rules -routes---App.jsx
import Home from 'Home'
import About from 'About'
import Services from 'Services'
import {Router,Route} from 'react-router-dom'

<Router>
<Route path='/' element={<Home/>} />
<Route path='/about' element={<About/>}/>
<Route path='/services' element={<Services/>}/>
</Router>

4) useNavigate - button
it is used for programatical routing
import {useNavigate} from 'react-router-dom'

let navigate=useNavigate()

<button onClick={()=>navigate('/')}>Home</button>
<button onClick={()=>navigate('/about')}>About</button>

dynamic routing


1) Routes in App.jsx


import Details from 'Details';

<Routes>
 <Route path='/details/:id' element={<Details/>}/>
</Routes>


2) useNavigate -button
let navigate=useNavigate()
<card>
 <button onClick={()=>navigate(`/details/${id}`)}> view details</button>
</card>


3) useParams 
it is used to get the dynamic data from url

import {useParams} from 'react-router-dom'

let {id}=useParams()



api calling
1) using fetch

await fetch(url)
await data.json()


2) using axios
1) 
npm install axios

2)-Home.jsx
import axios from 'axios';
import {useEffect,useState} from 'react'

let [doctors,setDoctors]=useState([])
useEffect(()=>{
fetchdata()
},[])

async function fetchdata(){
   let response=await axios.get('https://doctorapibackend.onrender.com/doctors')
   console.log(response.data)
   setDoctors(response.data)
}


